issue(id="0024" status="review")
  title Recover the partially published 0.1.12 release
  user-story
    as-a Release maintainer.
    i-want Reliable exact-version checks and a bounded recovery run.
    so-that Registry request failures cannot cause duplicate uploads or hide a partial release.
  premise.
    The 0.1.12 release published npm packages and puggers-core, then stopped after
    an opaque crates.io API visibility timeout. The historical HTTP failure is
    unknown. Recovery must use original source 3a5257f08e4a3d465d3be38ec826e8804add9522
    and the existing release.yml trusted publisher without credential changes.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Exact non-yanked sparse-index versions are skipped; confirmed absence permits publishing.
    criterion HTTP, transport, parsing, and yanked-version failures stop before uploading.
    criterion Missing crates pass locked Cargo dry runs and are verified after publishing.
    criterion Recovery only runs on main for 0.1.12, skips npm and core, and releases the original source.
  review-items
    item(status="covered") Regression tests cover present, absent, uncertain, and publishing failure paths.
    item(status="open") Approve merging the recovery workflow into main before dispatching it.
    item(status="open") Verify missing registry versions and the GitHub release after the recovery run.
